course: dictionary
lesson: 4756
title: One word, many hours
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An hour is a length of time, and it has sixty minutes. «Ruby stops games an hour before bed now» means she stops sixty minutes before bed. The words «before bed» tell you that hour is a measure of time.
explain: Hour can also mean a time of day, as in «at this hour». The words around it show which time is meant. In the plural, hours can mean when something is open or when someone works, as in «school hours» or «long hours» at work.
explain: Sometimes hour means a long time that nobody counted. «I waited for hours!» does not give an exact number. To check, swap in a number: if «I waited for two hours!» still makes sense, the first meaning is probably right.
fact: An hour has sixty minutes, so 2 hours is 120 minutes.
fact: A day has 24 hours.
fact: «Hours» can mean when a place is open, as in «school hours».
fact: «On the hour» means at 1:00, 2:00 and so on.
fact: «Hr» and «hrs» are short forms of hour and hours, often used in texts and timetables.
exercise: «Ruby stops games an hour before bed now.» How long is an hour? | Ten minutes | One day | Twenty-four minutes | *Sixty minutes
exercise: «Some high-paying jobs need long hours.» What do long hours mean here? | The distance to the office | Hours of sunshine on a beach | A very long clock | *The time someone spends working
exercise: Ella texts, «I waited hrs for the bus!» What does hrs mean? | *Hours, a short form of hour | Helpers | Hungry | Hard rock songs
test: «Kiritimati is 14 hours ahead of London.» How many minutes is 14 hours? | *840 minutes | 14 minutes | 1400 minutes | 140 minutes
test: A day has how many hours? | *24 | 100 | 60 | 12
exam: A train travels at a uniform rate of 60 kilometres per hour. How far does it travel in 3 hours? | 63 kilometres | 20 kilometres | 360 kilometres | *180 kilometres
